ode4.irmos:
O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation;
I have considered Thy works,//
and I have glorified Thy Divinity.

ode5.irmos2:
I rise at dawn unto Thee, the Creator of all, surpassing all worldly understanding;
for Thy commandments are light,//
wherein do Thou guide me.

ode6.irmos2:
The uttermost depths of sin have surrounded me, and my spirit perisheth;
but do Thou, O Master, stretch forth Thy lofty arm//
and like Peter save me, O my Helmsman.

ode7.irmos:
Once in Babylon the fire stood in awe of God's condescension;
for which sake the youths in the furnace, dancing with joyous steps as in a meadow, chanted://
O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!

ode8.irmos:
O ye Children, equal in number to the Trinity, bless ye God the Father and creator;
sing ye the praises of the Word Who descended and changed the fire into dew;
and exalt ye above all for ever//
the most Holy Spirit, Who giveth life unto all.
